libavformat/movenc: write the durations of a fragmented empty_moov file

With empty_moov the moov goes out before any sample, so its mvhd and tkhd
durations are zero and FFmpeg n6.0.1 writes no mehd: Media3 (which reads the
duration from mehd or tkhd) then sees an unknown duration even after a
normal stop, although the mfra makes the file seekable. When the trailer
has written the last fragment, write the real durations into those 32-bit
fields in place. Nothing moves, so the cost does not depend on the size of
the file, and a recording killed before the trailer keeps the zeros
(unknown duration) and stays readable. Outputs that cannot seek are left
as they were.

Modified by easiptv-ffmpeg on 2026-11-17, for the command line tool
(build-cli.sh) only: the audio decoder (build-decoder.sh) builds the
unmodified FFmpeg n6.0.1.

